
Linux on the ESP32-S31-WROOM-3-N16R16V: RV32 at 320 MHz, 16 MiB PSRAM.

Wi-Fi     wpa_passphrase "<ssid>" "<passphrase>" >> /etc/wpa_supplicant.conf
          /etc/init.d/S40wifi restart
          iw dev wlan0 link; iw dev wlan0 scan | grep SSID
Bluetooth bluetoothctl, then: scan le, scan bredr, devices
System    free, df -h, dmesg, mtdinfo
Network   ssh, scp, curl, iperf3
GPIO      gpiodetect, gpioinfo, gpioget, gpioset
Examples  ls /usr/share/examples
Storage   The root is writable and stays in the flash (UBIFS on /dev/mtd1).
          flash_erase /dev/mtd1 0 0, then reboot: back to the image.
